1
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Unforgotten, forever loved and adored.

2
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Evita is a history, drama film directed by Alan Parker.

3
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:36,000
The hit musical based on the life of Evita Duarte, an Argentinian actress who eventually became the wife
of Argentinian president Juan Perón, and the most beloved and hated woman in Argentina.

4
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Eva Perón, played by Madonna.

5
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:36,000
Ché, played by Antonio Banderas.

6
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
Juan Perón, played by Jonathan Pryce.

7
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Agustín Magaldi, played by Jimmy Nail.

8
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Doña Juana, played by Victoria Sus.

9
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:36,000
Brother Juan, played by Julian Littman.

10
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Evita is a 1996 American biographical musical drama film based on the 1978 stage musical by Tim
Rice and Andrew Lloyd Webber, which itself originated as a 1976 concept album.

11
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Directed by Alan Parker from a screenplay he co-wrote with Oliver Stone, the film depicts the life of Argentine
actress-turned-politician Eva Perón, detailing her beginnings, rise to power, and untimely death.

12
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
It stars Madonna in the title role, with Jonathan Pryce as her husband Juan Perón and
Antonio Banderas as Ché, an everyman who serves as the film's narrator.

13
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
A film adaptation of the musical languished in development for over fifteen years, as rights
passed on to several major studios, and various directors and actors considered.

14
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
In 1993, producer Robert Stigwood sold the rights to Andrew G.

15
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
Vajna, who agreed to finance the film through his production company Cinergi Pictures,
with Buena Vista Pictures distributing the film through Hollywood Pictures.

16
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
After Stone stepped down from the project in 1994,
Parker agreed to write and direct the film.

17
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
Recording sessions for the songs and soundtrack took place at CTS
Studios in London, roughly four months before filming.

18
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
Parker worked with Rice and Lloyd Webber to compose the soundtrack,
reworking the music and lyrics to the original songs.

19
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
They also wrote a new song, "You Must Love Me", for the film.

20
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
Principal photography commenced in February 1996
and concluded in May of that year.

21
01:34:30,000 --> 01:34:36,000
Filming took place on locations in Buenos Aires and Budapest as
well as on soundstages at Shepperton Studios.

22
01:39:00,000 --> 01:39:06,000
The film's production in Argentina was met with controversy, as the cast and crew
faced protests over fears that the project would tarnish Eva's image.

23
01:43:30,000 --> 01:43:36,000
Evita premiered at the Shrine Auditorium in Los
Angeles, California, on December 14, 1996.

24
01:48:00,000 --> 01:48:06,000
Hollywood Pictures gave the film a platform release, which involved releasing it in
select cities before expanding distribution in the following weeks.

25
01:52:30,000 --> 01:52:36,000
The film had a limited release on December 25, 1996,
before opening nationwide on January 10, 1997.

26
01:57:00,000 --> 01:57:06,000
It grossed $141 million worldwide against a $55 million budget and received mixed reviews; while Madonna's performance, the
music, costume designs, and cinematography were praised, criticism was aimed at the pacing and direction.

27
02:01:30,000 --> 02:01:36,000
Evita received numerous accolades, including the Academy Award for Best Original Song (for "You Must Love Me"), and three Golden Globe Awards:
Best Motion Picture – Comedy or Musical, Best Original Song ("You Must Love Me"), and Best Actress – Comedy or Musical (Madonna).

28
02:06:00,000 --> 02:06:06,000
The film explores themes of prostitute, funeral,
narration, buenos aires, argentina, politician.

29
02:10:30,000 --> 02:10:36,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
